          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You might have noticed that when you stand close to the plane mirror, the image also appears to be close to the mirror. The image appears to be far from the mirror when you stand far from the plane mirror."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.282,
            0.155,
            0.812,
            0.175
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Raise your left arm. Which arm does your image raise?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.282,
            0.178,
            0.825,
            0.198
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Touch your right ear. Which ear does your image touch?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.271,
            0.202,
            0.858,
            0.277
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You find that your left appears right in your image and your right appears left in your image. This type of perceived left-right reversal is called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "lateral inversion",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". There is lateral inversion in the images formed by a plane mirror."
            }
          ]
        },
